From 042db3fa8efb49df5040a31fee678daf944ecf8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:21:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Refuse an overwrite behind a recovery copy the log
 cannot sync, in both modes

A checkpoint's backfill, a format promotion, a conversion and the
invalid-state mark overwrite the data file behind a header journal and
WAL. With durable commits=false, a log that answered "cannot sync" (#2242)
let them proceed with that redo in the OS cache only, so a power loss mid
overwrite tore the data file (external review, point 1; decision D: the
strict rule protects the data file's integrity, not only recent commits).
The journal's barriers now refuse before the journal is written: a
checkpoint writes nothing and keeps the WAL (returning quietly, decision
5), a promotion or conversion is refused with the files unchanged. The WAL
limit holds while the log is known not to sync: no checkpoint can drain
the WAL then. With durable commits the barrier already threw.

Tests that pinned the old write-order behaviour are updated separately.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UFnsmor6qyZMSd1VoKwfJh
